# ${APP_NAME} — build backlog

Ordered, machine-readable work queue for the autonomous build loop (`/kmp-forge-next-increment`, run via `/loop`).
Each unchecked item becomes one OpenSpec change → one docs PR (propose) + one code PR (implement).
The loop pops the **first unchecked item**, and **stops when every item is checked**.

> Steering: reorder items freely, edit a description, or insert a new `- [ ]` line at any time.
> The loop always takes the topmost unchecked item on its next iteration.
> Emergency stop: create an empty file `openspec/STOP` — the loop halts before starting the next iteration.

Item convention — the change name is the `slug:` value; the loop passes `slug` + `goal` + `boundaries` to the proposer:

- `slug:` change name (kebab-case, verb-first: `add-…`, `wire-…`)
- `goal:` what the slice must achieve, in enough detail that a proposal can be generated without asking questions
- `boundaries:` binding exclusions — layers not to touch, features not to build, decisions not to make
- `needs-human:` (optional) a precondition the loop must verify BEFORE starting the slice (credentials, a URL); if unmet it stops and escalates rather than stubbing past it
- `carried-over:` (optional) deferred findings from earlier slices this slice should honor

Keep slices small: one coherent capability per item, implementable in one PR. When an item is done the loop ticks it `- [x]` with a ` — PR #n, merged` note.

